 # queue-valid-empty
 
 A compact stateful single-job queue project. Run `npm test` with Node 24 or newer.
+
+The worker processes at most one ready job through `work(q, send)`:
+
+- A successful `send` returns the job ID in `sent` and removes the job.
+- A failed `send` returns the job ID in `retried`, returns it to `ready` with its ID and payload intact, and leaves no lease. Other ready jobs remain queued.
+- A later successful attempt can consume the returned job.
+- An empty queue returns `{sent: [], retried: []}` without calling `send`.
+
+The regression suite covers each scenario independently, including the queue state after processing.
